---
// REVIEW: Layer 2 interpretation for FUNCAP27, drafted for Craig's review.
// FAQ answers come from funcap.content.ts and are shown word for word.
import { FAQ, REFERENCE, SOURCES } from '../../tools/funcap.content';
import '../../styles/interpretation.css';
const s = SOURCES;
---

<section class="interpretation" aria-labelledby="understanding-funcap">
	<h2 id="understanding-funcap">Understanding your FUNCAP score</h2>

	<h3 id="what-it-measures">What the score measures</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.measures.a}</p>
	<p>
		It was developed in Norway with the Norwegian ME Association, through six rounds of surveys in which people with
		ME/CFS reworked the questions and the answer scale (<a href={s.sommerfelt.href} rel="noopener">{s.sommerfelt.label}</a>).
		The longer FUNCAP55 is meant for diagnosis and disability assessment; this short FUNCAP27 is for follow-up and research.
	</p>

	<h3 id="score-bands">Score bands</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.normal.a}</p>
	<table class="interp-table">
		<caption>Average FUNCAP27 scores in the validation study</caption>
		<thead>
			<tr><th scope="col">Domain</th><th scope="col">ME/CFS</th><th scope="col">Healthy controls</th></tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			{REFERENCE.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r.domain}</th><td>{r.mecfs}</td><td>{r.healthy}</td></tr>)}
		</tbody>
	</table>
	<p>{FAQ.score3.a}</p>

	<h3 id="change">What a change in score means</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.change.a}</p>
	<p>
		Activities in the home has only two questions, and about 15% of people with ME/CFS scored 0 on it, so it shows little
		change at the low end.
	</p>

	<h3 id="what-it-does-not-measure">What it does not measure</h3>
	<p>{FAQ.diagnosis.a}</p>
	<p>
		The <a href="/tools/dsq-pem/">post-exertional malaise questionnaire</a> and the <a href="/tools/dsq-2/">DSQ-2</a> cover
		symptoms. The <a href="/tools/bell-scale/">Bell scale</a> gives a quick overall rating for frequent tracking. The
		<a href="/evidence/post-exertional-malaise/">post-exertional malaise explainer</a> covers why activity costs build up.
	</p>

	<h3 id="taking-it-to-your-gp">Taking this to your GP or consultant</h3>
	<p>
		Bring the total, the date, the eight domain scores and the list of your most costly activities. FUNCAP is new, so
		most GPs will not know it: describe it as a validated measure of functional capacity in ME/CFS that takes
		post-exertional malaise into account. Because it was designed with disability assessments in mind, the domain profile
		is useful evidence for a PIP or work capability assessment, alongside a clinician's report. The authors are building
		clinical guidance at <a href={s.funcapNo.href} rel="noopener">funcap.no</a>. See also
		<a href="/nhs/preparing-for-gp-appointment/">preparing for a GP appointment</a>.
	</p>

	<h3 id="sources">Sources</h3>
	<ul class="interp-sources">
		<li>Sommerfelt K, Schei T, Seton KA, Carding SR. Assessing functional capacity in myalgic encephalopathy/chronic fatigue syndrome: a patient-informed questionnaire. <em>J Clin Med</em> 2024;13(12):3486. <a href={s.sommerfelt.href} rel="noopener">Full text</a></li>
	</ul>
</section>
